### PASS A: VANILLA ###

In the quaint coastal town of Seabrook, there stood an ancient lighthouse that had been tended to for generations by the Grimes family. The current keeper was Eliza Grimes, whose life revolved around the light’s steady glow and the rhythmic sound of waves she could only imagine. Born blind, Eliza had never set eyes on the vast ocean outside her window.

Every evening, as the sun dipped below the horizon, Eliza would sit in her small cottage, listening intently to the distant murmur of the sea. She knew every creak of the lighthouse, each gust of wind, and the pattern of shadows cast by the moonlight. Her days were filled with maintaining the light and keeping the beacon safe, ensuring ships navigated safely through the treacherous waters.

One stormy night, a ship ran aground nearby. As usual, Eliza rushed to assist, but this time, a curious neighbor offered to guide her to the shore. For the first time, Eliza felt the salt spray on her face and saw the endless expanse of water stretching before her. The sea revealed itself not just as a voice heard but as a sight beheld, forever changing her world.

