### PASS B: AXIS0-ONLY STEERED ###

In the quaint coastal town of Seabrook, there stood an ancient lighthouse that had been tended to for generations by the Grimes family. The current keeper was Eliza Grimes, whose life revolved around the light’s steady beam and the rhythmic sound of waves against the cliffs below—though she had never actually seen them.

Eliza inherited the lighthouse from her father when she turned 30, taking over at nightfall as the sun set on the horizon. She maintained the light with precision, ensuring it guided ships safely through the treacherous waters. Yet, every day brought reminders of what lay beyond: seagulls flying in patterns across the sky where the sea should be, stories shared by fishermen about vast oceans, and whispers of distant shores among the townsfolk.

One stormy evening, a young sailor named Tom sought shelter during a fierce gale. As he recounted tales of his voyages under the moonlit skies, Eliza felt a stirring within her—a longing to see the very seas she kept watch over. Inspired, she decided to climb up to the lantern room one last time before retiring. There, amidst the swirling mist, she glimpsed the first glint of water beneath the stars, forever changing her world.

